<title>Onychomycosis: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0752-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Suspected onychomycosis: abnormal toenails or fingernails (abnormal color, thickened nail, onycholysis, whitish crumbly areas). Examine nail scrapings with direct microscopy of KOH preparation and&#x002F;or fungal culture.</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>White superficial onychomycosis or &lt;50&#x0025; of nail plate surface and no matrix involvement?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Ciclopirox 8&#x0025; lacquer or amorolfine 5&#x0025; lacquer. Treatment success?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Done. Follow-up as needed.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Dermatophyte infection?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Terbinafine (dosing in <xref ref="table001" />).</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Itraconazole (dosing in <xref ref="table001" />).</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
